FIX-02: Take no new segment for a link without flow

advectSegs() took a new segment from the pool for every link at every
quality step. For a link with no flow, evalnodeoutflow() returns before
using it and never gives it back, and the next step overwrites the pointer:
one segment and its concentration arrays leaked per zero-flow link per step
(about 70 MB per simulated week on Net6). MSX 1.1's release() gave the
segment back; the topological routing of 2.0 dropped that. Links without
flow now take no segment. Results are unchanged.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, on its own:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn FIX-02.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

diff --git a/src/solver/msxqual.c b/src/solver/msxqual.c
index 410ed5d..e73bd11 100644
--- a/src/solver/msxqual.c
+++ b/src/solver/msxqual.c
@@ -882,6 +882,16 @@ void advectSegs(double dt)
 
         for (m=1; m<=MSX.Nobjects[SPECIES]; m++) MSX.C1[m] = 0.0;
 
+    // --- a link with no flow releases no new segment over this time
+    //     step (evalnodeoutflow returns before using it), so don't take
+    //     one from the pool: it would never be returned to it
+
+        if ( MSX.Q[k] == 0.0 )
+        {
+            MSX.NewSeg[k] = NULL;
+            continue;
+        }
+
     // --- get a free segment to add to entrance of link
 
         MSX.NewSeg[k] = MSXqual_getFreeSeg(0.0, MSX.C1);
